    <string name="about_title">About &amp; help</string>
    <string name="about_version_fmt">Version %1$s (%2$d)</string>
    <string name="about_version_unknown">Version unknown</string>
    <string name="about_offline_promise">Offline by design: no network permission, account, or Keyic cloud. SQLCipher encrypts the local database. Argon2id and AES-GCM protect password-wrapped keys and encrypted backups. Exported files are under your control.</string>
    <string name="about_section_backup">Backup troubleshooting</string>
    <string name="about_help_backup">Link a folder and choose a sync passphrase. Automatic backups run only while the vault is unlocked; unavailable storage or a locked vault will be retried. Each successful backup creates a new file, keeping older copies. Manage old backups in your storage provider. Exports exclude the recycle bin. Restore replaces the current vault, including its recycle bin, so export a copy first. The .keyic file limit is 64 MB. Prefer .keyic for a complete Keyic backup; CSV excludes attachments and app-specific fields.</string>
    <string name="about_section_autofill">Autofill troubleshooting</string>
    <string name="about_help_autofill">Choose Keyic in Android Autofill settings. Store the exact website host or app package on each login entry; unrelated sites and lookalike names are not suggested. Card forms only use Card entries. Confirm the destination before filling: Keyic works offline and cannot verify website ownership or app signing identity. Use Other vault to switch and unlock another vault. Linked 2FA codes are copied when available.</string>
    <string name="about_section_lock">Lock &amp; clipboard</string>
    <string name="about_help_lock">Idle timeout and lock on leaving protect the vault. A system file picker may defer background locking until the idle timeout (up to 60 seconds when idle locking is disabled); reopen the operation after unlocking if needed. Clipboard clearing only removes the clip Keyic created. Android may block access in the background, so clearing is retried on return; process termination can prevent the timer from running. Biometrics require strong authentication; use the master password after enrollment changes or failures.</string>
    <string name="about_privacy_heading">Privacy</string>
    <string name="about_privacy_blurb">Full policy (opens in your browser — Keyic itself still has no network permission):</string>
    <string name="about_open_privacy">Open privacy policy</string>
